# Microsoft Graph API Permissions Policy

This rule enforces the exclusive use of **Delegated Permissions** for all Microsoft Graph API operations, with one specific exception.

## Core Principle

**ALWAYS use Delegated Permissions** - This MCP server operates on behalf of signed-in users and must request permissions that work in the user context.

## Permission Type Overview

| Permission Type | When to Use | This Project |
|-----------------|-------------|--------------|
| **Delegated** | User is signed in, app acts on their behalf | ✅ REQUIRED |
| **Application** | No user signed in (daemon/service) | ❌ FORBIDDEN |

## The Exception: User.Read.All

The **only** exception to the Delegated-only rule is:

```
User.Read.All (Application Permission)
```

### Why User.Read.All is Allowed as Application Permission

- Required for reading all user profiles in the organization
- Delegated version requires admin consent AND limits visibility
- Necessary for organizational directory lookups and user search features

## Permission Mapping Guidelines

### ✅ CORRECT: Use Delegated Permissions

```typescript
// User's own data
const DELEGATED_PERMISSIONS = {
  // Mail
  'Mail.Read': 'Read user mail',
  'Mail.ReadWrite': 'Read and write user mail',
  'Mail.Send': 'Send mail as user',
  
  // Calendar
  'Calendars.Read': 'Read user calendars',
  'Calendars.ReadWrite': 'Read and write user calendars',
  
  // Contacts
  'Contacts.Read': 'Read user contacts',
  'Contacts.ReadWrite': 'Read and write user contacts',
  
  // Files
  'Files.Read': 'Read user files',
  'Files.ReadWrite': 'Read and write user files',
  'Files.Read.All': 'Read all files user can access',
  'Files.ReadWrite.All': 'Read and write all files user can access',
  
  // User Profile
  'User.Read': 'Read user profile',
  'User.ReadBasic.All': 'Read basic profiles of all users',
  
  // Teams
  'Team.ReadBasic.All': 'Read teams the user is member of',
  'Channel.ReadBasic.All': 'Read channel names and descriptions',
  'Chat.Read': 'Read user chat messages',
  'Chat.ReadWrite': 'Read and write user chat messages',
  
  // Tasks
  'Tasks.Read': 'Read user tasks',
  'Tasks.ReadWrite': 'Create, read, update and delete user tasks',
  
  // Notes
  'Notes.Read': 'Read user OneNote notebooks',
  'Notes.ReadWrite': 'Read and write user OneNote notebooks',
  
  // Sites
  'Sites.Read.All': 'Read items in all site collections',
  'Sites.ReadWrite.All': 'Edit items in all site collections',
};
```

### ⚠️ EXCEPTION: Application Permission Allowed

```typescript
// ONLY exception - Application permission allowed
const APPLICATION_PERMISSION_EXCEPTION = {
  'User.Read.All': 'Read all user profiles (Application)',
};
```

### ❌ FORBIDDEN: Do Not Use These Application Permissions

```typescript
// NEVER use these as Application permissions
const FORBIDDEN_APPLICATION_PERMISSIONS = [
  'Mail.Read',           // Use Delegated instead
  'Mail.ReadWrite',      // Use Delegated instead
  'Mail.Send',           // Use Delegated instead
  'Calendars.Read',      // Use Delegated instead
  'Calendars.ReadWrite', // Use Delegated instead
  'Files.Read.All',      // Use Delegated instead
  'Files.ReadWrite.All', // Use Delegated instead
  'Chat.Read.All',       // Privacy violation
  'Chat.ReadWrite.All',  // Privacy violation
];
```

## Implementation Checklist

When implementing new Microsoft Graph API features:

- [ ] Identify required permissions from [Microsoft Graph permissions reference](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/graph/permissions-reference)
- [ ] Verify Delegated permission exists for the operation
- [ ] Use Delegated permission (NOT Application)
- [ ] Only use `User.Read.All` as Application permission if reading other users' profiles
- [ ] Document required permissions in tool description
- [ ] Update consent flow if new permissions needed

## Code Review Checklist

- [ ] No Application permissions used (except `User.Read.All`)
- [ ] Permissions follow least-privilege principle
- [ ] Permissions documented in tool definitions
- [ ] No over-scoped permissions (e.g., `.ReadWrite` when only `.Read` needed)

## Azure App Registration

When configuring the Azure AD App Registration:

```json
{
  "requiredResourceAccess": [
    {
      "resourceAppId": "00000003-0000-0000-c000-000000000000",
      "resourceAccess": [
        // Delegated Permissions (type: "Scope")
        { "id": "e1fe6dd8-ba31-4d61-89e7-88639da4683d", "type": "Scope" }, // User.Read
        { "id": "570282fd-fa5c-430d-a7fd-fc8dc98a9dca", "type": "Scope" }, // Mail.Read
        { "id": "024d486e-b451-40bb-833d-3e66d98c5c73", "type": "Scope" }, // Calendars.Read
        
        // ONLY Application Permission Exception
        { "id": "df021288-bdef-4463-88db-98f22de89214", "type": "Role" }  // User.Read.All (Application)
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

## Rationale

### Why Delegated Permissions?

1. **User Context**: MCP server operates on behalf of signed-in users
2. **Data Privacy**: Users only access their own data
3. **GDPR/DSGVO Compliance**: Minimizes data exposure
4. **Least Privilege**: Only access what the user can access
5. **Audit Trail**: Actions are attributable to specific users

### Why Exception for User.Read.All?

1. **Directory Lookup**: Required for finding users by email/name
2. **Meeting Attendees**: Need to resolve user profiles for calendar operations
3. **Organizational Features**: User search, people picker functionality
4. **No Delegated Equivalent**: Delegated `User.Read.All` is limited in scope

## Error Handling

If an operation fails due to missing permissions:

```typescript
// Check if operation requires forbidden permission
if (requiresApplicationPermission(operation) && operation !== 'readAllUsers') {
  throw new Error(
    `Operation "${operation}" requires Application permission which is not allowed. ` +
    `Use Delegated permission instead or refactor the approach.`
  );
}
```

